# Measured 2026-10-14 (run menu_b43, dolpic/0 dev start, 4:3, WARP, rc 0, 0 fatal): m_down2 shows PAUSE, the items
# つづける (selected, white) and セーブ (green), and the stage name ドルピニックタウン in the purple bubble;
# m_down4 shows the cursor back on つづける with the attention rays. Every glyph, including the small kana, is
# legible, so the console-string path (SMSGetMessageData bytes, not the balloon writer) is correct on the host.
# DOWN is the d-pad token; D_DOWN is not a token and makes the script stop.
# FontFix follow-up: the console strings of the pause menu (TConsoleStr path, not the talk balloon).
# The balloon writer is TGCConsole2::writeBalloonCodeTo; the pause menu text goes through the console string class,
# so it is the other 2D text path that a host-order bug would hit. dolpic/0, START opens the menu.
# Env: SUNSHINE_DEV_START=dolpic/0 SUNSHINE_DEV_SKIP_MOVIES=1 SUNSHINE_DEV_SEED=1 SUNSHINE_RENDER_SCALE=1
#   settings.ini [video] fsr1=0 widescreen=1 aspect=4:3
# Run: python tools/route.py Strict tools/routes/99_talk_text_menu.dev --name menu_b43 --seconds 240
# Evidence: m_*.png (menu text read from the PNG), 0 fatal, rc of the run.
waitfor director mario dirstate=4 camDemo=0 timeout=6000
wait frames=120
log
shot m_open.png
hold START frames=3
wait frames=90
log
shot m_p090.png
wait frames=30
shot m_p120.png
hold DOWN frames=3
wait frames=30
shot m_down1.png
hold DOWN frames=3
wait frames=30
shot m_down2.png
hold DOWN frames=3
wait frames=30
shot m_down3.png
hold DOWN frames=3
wait frames=30
shot m_down4.png
hold START frames=3
wait frames=60
log
end